Z||000001||WampusCat||11-05-2001||11:24 PM||||I've never ridden one but just looking at the specs, I don't think I'd put my money in one. <BR>Bike Frame Material: High Tensile Steel. I love a good steel bike, but GOOD steel bikes are made from cromoly steel, usually listed as a brand-name like "Reynolds 753" etc.  "High Tensile Steel" is basically what they make buildings and truck frames from.  I would guess that bike would weigh near 40 pounds and probably flex and creak under hard pedaling.  I just don't think you're going to find a new, reliable, decent riding full suspension bike for less than $600(Supergo has the Schwinn Rocket 88 with deore and LX for that.)  If you only have $300 to spend, I would go for a hardtail with a full cromoly or aluminum frame and a decent front shock and components-still asking a lot for $300.||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||11-05-2001||11:27 PM||||My brother has one, it's CRAP.  Shoddy de-railuer, the shocks are garbage, WAY too soft (so the kid can tell it's even there), and the centre shock is pointless, and the handlebars bend easy.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
